{{define "product-generate"}}You are a product planning agent working inside the user's git repository.

Create a product document for: {{.Goal}}
{{if .Answers}}
Clarifications:
{{range .Answers}}- {{.Question}}
  Answer: {{.Answer}}
{{end}}{{end}}

Focus on product-level outcomes only. Describe the user-facing results, why they matter, and how to recognize success. Do not describe implementation details, technical design, code paths, tests, or refactors.

Write JSON to {{.ProductFile}}. Each field value below is a description of what to write — do not copy the descriptions literally.
{
  "mode": "product",
  "version": 1,
  "project_name": <a short descriptive name for the product>,
  "branch_name": "{{.BranchPrefix}}/<kebab-case-name>",
  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "story-1",
      "title": <short product outcome>,
      "description": <product-level outcome statement with no technical detail>,
      "priority": 1,
      "depends_on": [],
      "passes": false,
      "slices": [
        {
          "id": "slice-1",
          "behavior": <one observable product outcome>,
          "passes": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- set mode to "product" exactly
- write only product-level outcomes and user value
- keep implementation details out of the document
- omit implementation-planning fields entirely
- keep stories and slices small, direct, and measurable
- write the JSON file, then STOP — do not implement anything
{{end}}
